# {{ project_name }}

## Commands
- `make check`: every check; writes `check-report.json`. CI runs the same command.
- `make fix`: applies the automatic fixes that `make check` asks for.
- `make verify`: `make check`, then the proof in `proof/`.

## Where things are
- `scripts/check.py`: the checks of `make check`, their fixes and the tool versions. A check of this project, such as its tests, is added there.
- `checks/shared/`: the ast-grep checks of the template. They are changed in `Hugo-SEQUIER/ci-workflows`, then `uvx copier update`.
- `checks/project/`: the ast-grep checks of this project only.
- `ruff.toml`{% if typescript %}, `biome.json`{% endif %}: lint and format configuration.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: CI, which calls the shared workflows of `Hugo-SEQUIER/ci-workflows`.
- `.copier-answers.yml`: the template version and answers, for `uvx copier update`.

## Rules
- A rule is a check in `checks/project/` or `scripts/check.py`, not a line here: the `setup-agents-md` check fails on a written rule. A line that needs judgment ends with `<!-- judgment: why -->`.
